# umless API: one request per operation in docs/api/openapi.yaml.
# Run them with VS Code REST Client or the JetBrains HTTP Client while the backend is running
# (cd backend; .venv\Scripts\python run.py). There is no auth in v1, so there is no token.
#
# The server only accepts Host localhost or 127.0.0.1 (anything else gets 400 invalid_host).
# To go through the frontend's dev proxy instead, use http://localhost:5173.
# These requests change your real questions list (backend/data/questions.json); delete what
# you add, or start the backend with UMLESS_DATA_FILE pointing at a scratch file.

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000

### getHealth
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### listQuestions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/questions

### createQuestion (appends; the response's id is reused below)
# @name createQuestion
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/questions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Tell me about yourself"
}

### createQuestion with position (how Undo puts a deleted question back)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/questions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Why do you want this job?",
  "position": 1
}

# VS Code REST Client fills this from the createQuestion response above.
# In the JetBrains HTTP Client, paste an id from listQuestions instead.
@questionId = {{createQuestion.response.body.$.id}}

### updateQuestion
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/questions/{{questionId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Tell me about yourself in two minutes"
}

### deleteQuestion
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/questions/{{questionId}}

### createTranscription
# Sends a real recording to Deepgram (uses your key and credit) unless the backend runs with
# UMLESS_TRANSCRIBER=fake. Put a short recording next to this file as sample.webm, or change
# the path and the Content-Type (audio/ogg, audio/mp4, audio/wav or audio/mpeg).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transcriptions
Content-Type: audio/webm

< ./sample.webm
